// ============================================================================
// AZURE BLOB STORAGE CONFIGURATION EXAMPLES
// ============================================================================

// ===========================================================================
// OPTION 1: DEVELOPMENT (Using Connection String)
// ===========================================================================
// Recommended for local development
// Authentication: Storage Account Access Key
// Setup: Get connection string from Azure Portal → Storage Account → Access Keys
//
// Steps:
// 1. Get connection string from Azure Portal
// 2. Set via user-secrets: 
//    dotnet user-secrets set "BlobStorage:ConnectionString" "DefaultEndpointsProtocol=..."
// 3. Use appsettings.Development.json below
//

{
  "BlobStorage": {
    // ✅ Use connection string for development
    "ConnectionString": "DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=your-account;AccountKey=your-key;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net",

    // Set to false when using ConnectionString
    "UseManagedIdentity": false,

    // Container name (will be created if AutoCreateContainer is true)
    "ContainerName": "screenshots",

    // How long SAS URLs are valid (in minutes)
    "SasUrlExpirationMinutes": 60,

    // Auto-create container if it doesn't exist
    "AutoCreateContainer": true
  }
}

// ===========================================================================
// OPTION 2: PRODUCTION (Using Managed Identity)
// ===========================================================================
// Recommended for apps running in Azure
// Authentication: Azure Managed Identity (System-Assigned or User-Assigned)
// Setup: No connection string needed, relies on Azure RBAC
//
// Steps:
// 1. Create managed identity in Azure
// 2. Assign "Storage Blob Data Contributor" role to the identity
// 3. Use configuration below
// 4. Deploy app with managed identity binding
//

{
  "BlobStorage": {
    // Use account name (NOT the full domain)
    "AccountName": "your-storage-account",

    // Set to true to use Managed Identity / DefaultAzureCredential
    "UseManagedIdentity": true,

    // Container name
    "ContainerName": "screenshots",

    // How long SAS URLs are valid (in minutes)
    "SasUrlExpirationMinutes": 60,

    // Auto-create container if it doesn't exist
    "AutoCreateContainer": true
  }
}

// ===========================================================================
// OPTION 3: LOCAL TESTING WITH AZURE STORAGE EMULATOR
// ===========================================================================
// For completely offline development
// Requires: Azure Storage Emulator installed
// Start emulator before running the app
//

{
  "BlobStorage": {
    "ConnectionString": "UseDevelopmentStorage=true",
    "UseManagedIdentity": false,
    "ContainerName": "screenshots",
    "SasUrlExpirationMinutes": 60,
    "AutoCreateContainer": true
  }
}

// ===========================================================================
// CONFIGURATION REFERENCE
// ===========================================================================

/*
Field: ConnectionString
Type: string (optional)
Usage: When UseManagedIdentity = false
Format: DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=XXXX;AccountKey=YYYY;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net
Where to get: Azure Portal → Storage Accounts → Your Account → Access Keys → Connection String (key1)
Note: Store in user-secrets, NOT in appsettings
Default: null

Field: AccountName
Type: string (optional)
Usage: When UseManagedIdentity = true, OR for connection string format
Format: Just the account name (e.g., "mystorageaccount", NOT "mystorageaccount.blob.core.windows.net")
Where to get: Azure Portal → Storage Accounts → Your Account name
Note: Required when using Managed Identity
Default: null

Field: ContainerName
Type: string (required)
Usage: Name of the blob container to store screenshots
Format: Lowercase alphanumeric, no spaces or special chars (except hyphens)
Value: Use "screenshots" (or customize if needed)
Default: "screenshots"

Field: UseManagedIdentity
Type: boolean
Usage: Choose authentication method
Values:
  - true: Use Azure Managed Identity (recommended for Azure-hosted apps)
  - false: Use Connection String (recommended for local development)
Default: true

Field: SasUrlExpirationMinutes
Type: integer (must be > 0)
Usage: How long generated SAS URLs are valid
Recommended: 60 minutes (1 hour)
Range: 1 to 1440+ minutes
Default: 60

Field: AutoCreateContainer
Type: boolean
Usage: Automatically create container if it doesn't exist
Values:
  - true: Container is created on first app run
  - false: Container must exist before app starts
Note: Creating requires "Storage Blob Data Contributor" role
Default: true
*/

// ===========================================================================
// USER-SECRETS SETUP EXAMPLES
// ===========================================================================

/*
PowerShell:

# Set connection string (development)
dotnet user-secrets set "BlobStorage:ConnectionString" "DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=mystorageacct;AccountKey=ABC123==;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net"

# Set account name (production / managed identity)
dotnet user-secrets set "BlobStorage:AccountName" "mystorageacct"
dotnet user-secrets set "BlobStorage:UseManagedIdentity" "true"

# Verify secrets
dotnet user-secrets list

# Clear all secrets
dotnet user-secrets clear

bash/zsh:

# Set connection string (development)
dotnet user-secrets set "BlobStorage:ConnectionString" "DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=mystorageacct;AccountKey=ABC123==;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net"

# Set account name (production / managed identity)
dotnet user-secrets set "BlobStorage:AccountName" "mystorageacct"
dotnet user-secrets set "BlobStorage:UseManagedIdentity" "true"

# Verify secrets
dotnet user-secrets list
*/

// ===========================================================================
// VALIDATION LOGIC
// ===========================================================================

/*
The app validates configuration on startup and will throw an exception if:

1. UseManagedIdentity = true AND AccountName is empty/null
   → Error: "AccountName is required when UseManagedIdentity is true."
   → Fix: Set AccountName in config or user-secrets

2. UseManagedIdentity = false AND ConnectionString is empty/null
   → Error: "ConnectionString is required when UseManagedIdentity is false."
   → Fix: Set ConnectionString in appsettings or user-secrets

3. ContainerName is empty/null
   → Error: "ContainerName is required."
   → Fix: Set ContainerName (default is "screenshots")

4. SasUrlExpirationMinutes <= 0
   → Error: "SasUrlExpirationMinutes must be greater than 0."
   → Fix: Use positive integer (recommended: 60)
*/

// ===========================================================================
// ERROR RECOVERY
// ===========================================================================

/*
If app fails to start with configuration errors:

1. Check the error message for exactly what's missing
2. Look at examples above that match your scenario
3. Set the missing configuration value
4. Restart the app

For connection string issues:
- Regenerate in Azure Portal: Storage Account → Access Keys → Rotate key
- Copy the FULL connection string (not just the key)
- Set via user-secrets (not in appsettings files)

For managed identity issues:
- Verify identity is assigned to the app (App Service → Identity)
- Verify "Storage Blob Data Contributor" role is assigned
- Run: az role assignment list --assignee <identity-id>
- Container must exist or AutoCreateContainer must be true
*/

